From 6ff2f24a5702b6fc28120f6aef27e1030f2aedf2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kugan Vivekanandarajah <kvivekananda@nvidia.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 22:35:24 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 32/45] Wire afdo-tools into the GCC build

Register afdo-tools as an optional bootstrapped GCC host module and
regenerate the top-level build files.  The module is configured on
GNU/Linux hosts only, is skipped when testing a cross compiler, and is
ordered after the host dependencies it needs.  Its sources are added to the
list scanned for translatable strings.

ChangeLog:

	* Makefile.def (host_modules): Add afdo-tools as a bootstrapped
	host module and skip its checks for cross builds.
	(dependencies): Order afdo-tools after configure-gcc and gettext and
	GCC after afdo-tools.
	* Makefile.tpl (check-[+module+]): Continue the native-only check
	command onto its closing fi.
	* Makefile.in: Regenerate.
	* configure.ac: Configure afdo-tools on GNU/Linux hosts only.
	* configure: Regenerate.

gcc/po/ChangeLog:

	* exgettext: Scan ../afdo-tools/src for translatable strings.

Signed-off-by: Kugan Vivekanandarajah <kvivekananda@nvidia.com>
Co-authored-by: Dhruv Chawla <dhruvc@nvidia.com>
Co-authored-by: Rahul Shinde <rashinde@nvidia.com>
