From 5c1384a623fdc77c1a621ff00bdf9595114b7850 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dhruv Chawla <dhruvc@nvidia.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 22:35:26 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 34/45] Use in-tree tools for profile bootstrap

Switch autoprofiledbootstrap and DejaGnu AutoFDO profile generation from
the external create_gcov/profile_merger tools to in-tree afdo_create and
afdo_merge while retaining the existing CREATE_GCOV and PROFILE_MERGER
variable names.  When the module is disabled, find the tools on PATH.

Add AFDO_GCOV_VERSION so callers can select the generated profile format.
When it is unset, query the stage1 compiler for its supported format.
Resolve relative CREATE_GCOV values against the GCC build directory in
profopt.exp, and compare afdo-tools normally because every stage builds it
from the same sources.  An unsampled lto1 uses an empty profile.

ChangeLog:

	* Makefile.tpl (CREATE_GCOV): Select in-tree or PATH afdo_create by default.
	(PROFILE_MERGER): Select in-tree or PATH afdo_merge by default.
	(AFDO_GCOV_VERSION): New variable.
	(EXTRA_HOST_FLAGS): Pass it.
	* Makefile.in: Regenerate.

gcc/ChangeLog:

	* Makefile.in (AFDO_GCOV_VERSION_ARG): New variable.
	(all.fda): Use it.

gcc/c/ChangeLog:

	* Make-lang.in (cc1.fda, create_fdas_for_cc1): Use CREATE_GCOV
	and AFDO_GCOV_VERSION_ARG.

gcc/cp/ChangeLog:

	* Make-lang.in (cc1plus.fda, create_fdas_for_cc1plus): Use
	CREATE_GCOV and AFDO_GCOV_VERSION_ARG.

gcc/lto/ChangeLog:

	* Make-lang.in (lto1.fda, create_fdas_for_lto1): Use CREATE_GCOV
	and AFDO_GCOV_VERSION_ARG.  Allow an empty profile when unsampled.

gcc/testsuite/ChangeLog:

	* lib/profopt.exp (profopt-execute): Honour AFDO_GCOV_VERSION and
	resolve CREATE_GCOV against the GCC build directory.  Remove stale
	profiles and check the converter exit status.

Signed-off-by: Dhruv Chawla <dhruvc@nvidia.com>
Co-authored-by: Kugan Vivekanandarajah <kvivekananda@nvidia.com>
Co-authored-by: Rahul Shinde <rashinde@nvidia.com>
