From 101ab13cc2111d30508e9788cfdcde16db28fc0f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dhruv Chawla <dhruvc@nvidia.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 22:35:27 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 35/45] Add GCOV v4 read/write machinery

Add section-based GCOV AutoFDO v4 profile I/O to afdo_tools:

  - extend the shared profile model for v4 sections
  - add gcov_reader_v4 and gcov_writer_v4 for binary and text
  - teach the reader and writer factories to select v3 or v4

Existing afdo_dump, afdo_merge and afdo_create consume v4 through the
factories without format-specific call sites.  Compiler-side consumption
is added in the next patch.

V4 has a self-describing, fixed-width section directory.  Section bodies
use varints while the header, directory and string-trie framing remain
fixed-width little-endian.  Reverse inline-index sections let a partial
reader load cross-module inliners without materializing every function.

Preserve the independent call-site count as well as its target counts in
binary and text profiles.  Quote and escape every string in text profiles
so paths and symbols round-trip without ambiguity.

Validate section bounds and types, symbol ranges, referenced symbol ids,
varint widths and count-driven allocations before decoding.  In particular,
bound reverse-inline-index traversal by the section size.

Add binary, text and partial-read unit coverage for call counts, quoted
strings, cross-file inliners and overflowing varints.  Run the DejaGnu
tests with v3, v4 binary and v4 text output.

Regression tested on aarch64-linux-gnu with no new regressions.

afdo-tools/ChangeLog:

	* Makefile.in: Build the v4 reader, writer and unit test.  Run the
	unit test from check.
	* src/afdo_create.cc (write_gcov_output): Select the output writer
	through make_gcov_writer.
	(parse_arguments): Validate text output before profiling.
	* src/afdo_dump.cc (main): Accept and dump v4 profiles.
	* src/afdo_merge.cc (main): Accept v3 and v4 inputs and select the
	output version and format.
	* src/gcov.h: Extend the profile model for GCOV v4.
	* src/gcov_io.cc: Add v4 I/O primitives and validate varints.
	* src/gcov_io.h: Declare the v4 I/O primitives.
	* src/gcov_merge.cc (gcov_merger): Merge v4 profile data.
	* src/gcov_merge.h: Likewise.
	* src/gcov_reader.cc (make_gcov_reader): Detect and construct the v4
	reader for binary and text profiles.
	* src/gcov_reader.h: Declare gcov_reader_v4 and multi-file partial reads.
	* src/gcov_reader_v4.cc: New file.  Support multi-file partial reads.
	* src/gcov_writer.cc (make_gcov_writer): Construct the v4 writer.
	* src/gcov_writer.h: Declare gcov_writer_v4.
	* src/gcov_writer_v4.cc: New file.
	* testsuite/afdo-test/afdo-test.exp: Run each test with every GCOV
	encoding.
	* testsuite/lib/afdo.exp (afdo_format_flags, afdo_current_format,
	afdo_expand_formats, afdo_forced_format_flags): New.
	(afdo_check_determinism, afdo_create_gcov, afdo_create_live,
	afdo_run_instance, afdo_run_merge_instance): Use the selected format.
	* testsuite/unit/gcov-v4-test.cc: New test.

