From fef6f694603b2ac6cc8f320ab0ee2bcbe4bbc7e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kugan Vivekanandarajah <kvivekananda@nvidia.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 22:35:29 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 37/45] Document afdo-tools in install.texi

Document --enable-afdo-tools, the host and library requirements, and the
use of the in-tree tools by autoprofiledbootstrap.

gcc/ChangeLog:

	* doc/install.texi: Document --enable-afdo-tools and update the
	AutoFDO tool requirement for autoprofiledbootstrap.

Signed-off-by: Kugan Vivekanandarajah <kvivekananda@nvidia.com>
---
 gcc/doc/install.texi | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/gcc/doc/install.texi b/gcc/doc/install.texi
index 001d16fe67a..94cf91836c2 100644
--- a/gcc/doc/install.texi
+++ b/gcc/doc/install.texi
@@ -1297,6 +1297,21 @@ one or more @code{.sarif} files as input and attempts to replay any
 diagnostics within them to stderr (via @code{libgdiagnostics}) in the style
 of GCC's diagnostics.
 
+@item --enable-afdo-tools
+Build the @file{afdo-tools} directory, which provides the host tools
+@command{afdo_create}, @command{afdo_dump} and @command{afdo_merge}.
+@command{afdo_create} turns Linux @command{perf} samples into an AutoFDO
+profile for use with @option{-fauto-profile}, @command{afdo_merge}
+combines such profiles and @command{afdo_dump} prints one in readable
+form.  They are also used by @samp{make autoprofiledbootstrap} and by the
+AutoFDO tests in the testsuite.
+
+The module is supported on 64-bit little-endian GNU/Linux hosts with
+@code{perf_event_open} and a compatible @file{linux/perf_event.h}.
+It requires @code{libelf}, @code{libdw} and @code{zlib}.  The tools run
+on the host and do not depend on the target that GCC is configured for.
+@option{--disable-afdo-tools} is the default.
+
 @item --disable-gcov
 Specify that the run-time library used for coverage analysis
 and associated host tools should not be built.
@@ -3496,8 +3511,11 @@ On Linux/x86_64 hosts with some restrictions (no virtualization) it is
 also possible to do autofdo build with @samp{make
 autoprofiledbootstrap}. This uses Linux perf to sample branches in the
 binary and then rebuild it with feedback derived from the profile.
-Linux perf and the @code{autofdo} toolkit needs to be installed for
-this.
+Linux perf needs to be installed for this, together with the AutoFDO
+profile tools: either the in-tree ones enabled by
+@option{--enable-afdo-tools}, or the out-of-tree @code{autofdo}
+toolkit, selected with the @code{CREATE_GCOV} and @code{PROFILE_MERGER}
+make variables and @code{AFDO_GCOV_VERSION=3}.
 
 Only the profile from the current build is used, so when an error
 occurs it is recommended to clean before restarting. Otherwise
-- 
