From 368563b2cff748e580a5429a3b85320f4d2d758c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kugan Vivekanandarajah <kvivekananda@nvidia.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 11:02:22 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 42/45] [AutoFDO] Keep a local IPA-CP profile under
 -fprofile-partial-training

When the callers of a new clone already claim more count than the original
node, update_profiling_info lowers the original's profile.  The comment
says to lower it to global0adjusted, or to local under partial training,
but both branches ran: make_profile_local was immediately overwritten by
make_profile_global0.

gcc/ChangeLog:

	* ipa-cp.cc (update_profiling_info): Under
	-fprofile-partial-training lower the original node's profile to
	local instead of also forcing it to global0.

(cherry picked from commit f40ee73f6e7d50608d7a464e57ce2000ae5d0014)
---
 gcc/ipa-cp.cc | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/gcc/ipa-cp.cc b/gcc/ipa-cp.cc
index e746ff0ede3..6b4a3713ffe 100644
--- a/gcc/ipa-cp.cc
+++ b/gcc/ipa-cp.cc
@@ -4817,7 +4817,7 @@ update_profiling_info (struct cgraph_node *orig_node,
 	 to global0adjusted or to local if we have partial training.  */
       if (opt_for_fn (orig_node->decl, flag_profile_partial_training))
 	orig_node->make_profile_local ();
-      if (new_sum.quality () == AFDO)
+      else if (new_sum.quality () == AFDO)
 	orig_node->make_profile_global0 (GUESSED_GLOBAL0_AFDO);
       else
 	orig_node->make_profile_global0 (GUESSED_GLOBAL0_ADJUSTED);
-- 
