From ca966a723330734b8214d7ef81cf67acc9e3bc84 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artemiy Volkov <artemiy.volkov@arm.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 14:05:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 44/45] profile_probability: two fixes for ->sqrt ()

Firstly, so far, we've always been returning 'm_val' from this method (which is
the input value of the algorithm) rather than 'val' (which is the value of the
result).  Fix that so we get correct values out of ->sqrt ().

Additionally, change the while loop condition on l. 511 to avoid an
unrecoverable infinite loop whenever min_range ends up being greater than
max_range due to precision errors.

Bootstrapped and regtested on aarch64-linux-gnu and x86_64-linux-gnu.  OK for
trunk and/or backports?

gcc/ChangeLog:

	* profile-count.cc (profile_probability::sqrt): Return val
	instead of m_val.  Alter the while loop condition.

(cherry picked from commit 1123e52e811349dc880a5fc1abe4d5d427fcf70c)
---
 gcc/profile-count.cc | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/gcc/profile-count.cc b/gcc/profile-count.cc
index 2cce9caa772..ee20aa18289 100644
--- a/gcc/profile-count.cc
+++ b/gcc/profile-count.cc
@@ -507,12 +507,12 @@ profile_probability::sqrt () const
     max_range = 0;
   if (m_val == max_probability)
     min_range = max_probability;
-  while (min_range != max_range)
+  while (min_range < max_range)
     {
       uint32_t val = (min_range + max_range) / 2;
       uint32_t val2 = RDIV ((uint64_t)val * val, max_probability);
       if (val2 == m_val)
-	min_range = max_range = m_val;
+	min_range = max_range = val;
       else if (val2 > m_val)
 	max_range = val - 1;
       else if (val2 < m_val)
